st place  a big change since the last forum which  a lot of people  will remember is the man in the white  house do you think  that having joe biden as president of  the united states has  made the tone somewhat different this  year  a new administration means big changes  for everyone  and uh you know joe biden is no stranger  to  the world economic forum he's been with  us as vice president a couple of times  he's been to other meetings that we've  held around the world  so you know we know the president and uh  you know we're looking forward to  working with him we had john kerry his  climate czar speaking this week  on the plans that the united states has  to really  get back behind the wheel in terms of  driving  uh the agenda on climate change so i do  think there's a whole number of  different ways in which this  administration  will make a difference but it's not just  the us you know i think one of the  things we've seen  through the crisis is that every single  major economy has a role to play  and i think hearing from those leaders  and seeing that we're now in  very much a multi-polar world has been a  big part  of what davos this week online has been  about  yes it has been online it's been without  the the private jets and all the  trappings of the usual  davos agreement davos this year could  this online  wef be here to stay  funnily enough uh you know you say that  but actually private jet traffic into  davos is known more than during a busy  week in zurich  art fair uh in actual fact emissions in  davos the town  go down during davos week so the air is  cleaner  purer and nicer when we're in town than  when the locals  are left to themselves with buses cars  and everything running through the  center of their lovely  alpine uh town but  uh it has made a difference to us in one  very important way it's enabled us to  bring in  many many more people into these  conversations and you know the impact  online  has been enormous it's something like  five 